      "raw_response": "Abstract: This abstract supports the claim.\n\nThe study presents evidence that PDS treatment significantly decreases the replication efficiency of G-rich telomeric repeats in BRCA2-deficient cells, linking G4 formation to telomere instability. It demonstrates that PDS promotes DSB accumulation and checkpoint activation in HR-defective cells, leading to G2/M deregulation. Additionally, it shows that PDS can enhance replication defects in cells that have developed olaparib resistance. These findings suggest that G4-stabilizing drugs like PDS could target and eliminate HR-compromised cells, including those resistant to PARP inhibition. (Confidence level: high)\n\nANSWER: Supported.",
