      "raw_response": "SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract supports the claim that pyridostatin encourages proliferation of homologous recombination (HR) defective cells. The abstract states that PDS reduces proliferation of HR-defective cells by inducing DSB accumulation, checkpoint activation, and deregulated G2/M progression, indicating that pyridostatin has a negative effect on HR defective cells. Additionally, it mentions that PDS toxicity extends to HR-defective cells that have acquired resistance to olaparib, further supporting the idea that pyridostatin encourages proliferation of HR defective cells.",
